<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="sec-examples-remarks" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Examples and Remarks</title>
  <example xml:id="ex-gcd">
    <title>A Greatest Common Divisor</title>
    <idx><h>greatest common divisor</h></idx>
    <statement>
      <p>Find the greatest common divisor of <m>48</m> and <m>18</m>.</p>
    </statement>
    <solution>
      <p>Repeated division gives</p>
      <md>
        <mrow>48 \amp= 2 \cdot 18 + 12</mrow>
        <mrow>18 \amp= 1 \cdot 12 + 6</mrow>
        <mrow>12 \amp= 2 \cdot 6 + 0</mrow>
      </md>.
      <p>The last nonzero remainder is <m>6</m>, so <m>\gcd(48,18) = 6</m>.</p>
    </solution>
  </example>
  <example xml:id="ex-not-prime">
    <statement>
      <p>The number <m>91</m> is not prime, because <m>91 = 7 \cdot 13</m>.</p>
    </statement>
  </example>
  <remark xml:id="rem-primes">
    <title>On Primes</title>
    <p>The primes below <m>20</m> are <m>2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19</m>.</p>
  </remark>
  <note xml:id="note-two">
    <title>An Even Prime</title>
    <p>The number <m>2</m> is the only even prime.</p>
  </note>
</section>